# A modded-nanogpt-style speedrun recipe (Keller Jordan et al., 2024-25) on its
# architecture, which comes from examples/architectures/ by name. Approximate: the
# record runs give the embedding, the head and the scalars Adam learning rates of their
# own, and change the sequence length and Muon's momentum during the run.
#
# The data is the FineWeb slice the speedrun's shards come from, as Parquet files:
#
#   hf download HuggingFaceFW/fineweb --repo-type dataset \
#       --include "sample/10BT/*" --local-dir data/fineweb
#   bux prepare examples/experiments/speedrun.bux  # tokenized and packed once, ~10B tokens
#   bux train examples/experiments/speedrun.bux
#
# GPT-2 tokens, every document after an <|endoftext|>, as in the shards. Best-fit
# packing starts every row at a document and keeps documents whole, each seeing only
# itself, as the record runs' BOS-aligned batches do. A hundredth is held out.
use modded_nanogpt

tokenizer = tokenizer(name="gpt2")
fineweb   = text(path="data/fineweb/sample/10BT/*.parquet", bos=true, eos=false)
packing   = best_fit

data      = fineweb(split=[0, 0.99])
optimizer = muon(lr=0.05, consistent_rms=none,
                 adam=adamw(lr=0.008, b1=0.8, weight_decay=0))
schedule  = wsd(decay=0.4)
seq_len   = 1024
batch     = 8 * 64                   # 8 GPUs, 64 rows each
steps     = 1750

eval       = eval(data=fineweb(split=[0.99, 1]), every=125, batches=20)
checkpoint = checkpoint(every=500)
